    19→---
    20→
    21→# Retro LaTeX-Style PDF Generation
    22→
    23→Convert markdown documents to professional, retro LaTeX-style PDFs with academic formatting.
    24→
    25→## Features
    26→
    27→- **LaTeX/Academic styling** - Libre Baskerville font (similar to Computer Modern), tight paragraph spacing
    28→- **Clickable Table of Contents** - Auto-generated TOC with anchor links to all sections
    29→- **Geek Corner / Example Corner boxes** - Open-ended table style with horizontal rules (title separated from content by thin line)
    30→- **Academic tables** - Horizontal rules only, italic headers, no vertical borders
    31→- **Full references section** - Proper citations with clickable URLs
    32→- **No headers/footers** - Clean pages without date/time stamps
    33→
    34→## Usage
    35→
    36→When the user asks to convert a markdown document to a retro/LaTeX-style PDF, follow this process:
    37→
    38→### Step 1: Create the HTML Template
    39→
