   282→```
   283→
   284→### Step 2: Structure the Content
   285→
   286→#### Title and Subtitle
   287→```html
   288→<h1>Document Title</h1>
   289→<p class="subtitle">Subtitle or tagline in italics</p>
   290→<hr>
   291→```
   292→
   293→#### Table of Contents
   294→```html
   295→<div class="toc">
   296→  <div class="toc-title">Contents</div>
   297→  <ul>
   298→    <li class="toc-h2"><a href="#sec1">1. Section Title</a></li>
   299→    <li class="toc-h3"><a href="#sec1-1">1.1 Subsection Title</a></li>
   300→    <!-- ... more entries ... -->
   301→    <li class="toc-h2"><a href="#references">References</a></li>
   302→  </ul>
   303→</div>
   304→<hr>
   305→```
   306→
   307→#### Section Headings (with anchor IDs)
   308→```html
   309→<h2 id="sec1">1. Section Title</h2>
   310→<h3 id="sec1-1">1.1 Subsection Title</h3>
   311→<h4>Step 1: Sub-subsection (italic)</h4>
   312→```
   313→
   314→#### Geek Corner / Example Corner Box
   315→```html
   316→<div class="geek-corner">
   317→  <div class="geek-corner-top">
   318→    <span class="geek-corner-title">Geek Corner: Title Here</span>
   319→  </div>
   320→  <div class="geek-corner-bottom">
   321→    <span class="geek-corner-content">"The witty or insightful quote goes here in italics."</span>
   322→  </div>
   323→</div>
   324→```
   325→
   326→#### Tables (Academic Style)
   327→```html
   328→<table>
   329→  <tr>
   330→    <th>Column 1</th>
   331→    <th>Column 2</th>
   332→    <th>Column 3</th>
   333→  </tr>
   334→  <tr>
   335→    <td>Data</td>
   336→    <td>Data</td>
   337→    <td>Data</td>
   338→  </tr>
   339→</table>
   340→```
   341→
   342→#### Footnote References (in text)
   343→```html
   344→<sup><a href="#ref1">[1]</a></sup>
   345→```
   346→
   347→#### References Section
   348→```html
   349→<hr>
   350→<h2 id="references">References</h2>
   351→<div class="footnote" style="border-top: none; margin-top: 10px; padding-top: 0;">
   352→  <p id="ref1"><strong>[1]</strong> Author, Name. "Article Title." Publication (Year). <a href="https://url.com" target="_blank">https://url.com</a> - Brief description.</p>
   353→  <p id="ref2"><strong>[2]</strong> ...</p>
   354→</div>
   355→```
   356→
   357→#### Key Takeaway
   358→```html
   359→<p class="key-takeaway"><strong>Key Takeaway:</strong> Important summary text here.</p>
   360→```
   361→
   362→### Step 3: Generate the PDF
   363→
   364→Use Chrome headless to generate the PDF without headers/footers:
   365→
   366→```bash
   367→"/Applications/Google Chrome.app/Contents/MacOS/Google Chrome" \
   368→  --headless \
   369→  --disable-gpu \
   370→  --print-to-pdf="/path/to/output.pdf" \
   371→  --print-to-pdf-no-header \
   372→  --no-pdf-header-footer \
   373→  "file:///path/to/input.html"
   374→```
   375→
   376→On Linux:
   377→```bash
   378→google-chrome --headless --disable-gpu --print-to-pdf="/path/to/output.pdf" --print-to-pdf-no-header --no-pdf-header-footer "file:///path/to/input.html"
   379→```
   380→
   381→## Style Guidelines
   382→
   383→1. **Paragraphs**: Keep text dense and justified. Collapse bullet points into flowing prose where appropriate.
   384→
   385→2. **Geek Corner**: Use for witty asides, technical insights, or memorable quotes. Always include:
   386→   - A catchy title (e.g., "Geek Corner: Amdahl's Law, App Edition")
   387→   - Italic content in quotes
   388→
   389→3. **Tables**: Use sparingly for data comparisons. Always use the open style (horizontal rules only).
   390→
   391→4. **References**: Always include full citations with:
   392→   - Author name
   393→   - Article/document title in quotes
   394→   - Publication/source and year
   395→   - Full clickable URL
   396→   - Brief description of what the reference covers
   397→
   398→5. **Spacing**: Keep tight - 6px paragraph margins, 1.35 line height.
   399→

